cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Advanced Python and SQL for Applied Economic & Financial Analysis
  (Durham MSc Economics)
message: "If you use these course materials, please cite them as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sitraka
    family-names: Forler
    email: sitraka.forler@post.lu
    affiliation: "POST Luxembourg; IAE Metz; Centrale Méditerranée (AMU)"
abstract: >-
  A two-day, hands-on workshop teaching Python and SQL for applied economic
  analysis, built around the question "Did the Fed's 2022–23 tightening cycle
  work?". Uses real FRED, World Bank and OECD data, runs zero-install in GitHub
  Codespaces, and includes a local machine-learning module (scikit-learn).
keywords:
  - economics
  - python
  - sql
  - machine-learning
  - monetary-policy
  - teaching-materials
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sitraka17/durham-python-sql-2026"
url: "https://github.com/Sitraka17/durham-python-sql-2026"
